## Occurrences by Sense

### Throne-room agents dispatched for earth-patrol (Zechariah visions)
- {{ref:Zec.1.8}} — red horse + rider among myrtle trees; red, speckled, white horses behind
- {{ref:Zec.1.10}} — "these are they whom the LORD hath sent to walk to and fro"
- {{ref:Zec.1.11}} — report: "all the earth sitteth still, and is at rest"
- {{ref:Zec.6.1}} — four chariots from between two mountains of brass
- {{ref:Zec.6.2-3}} — red, black, white, grisled + bay horses
- {{ref:Zec.6.5}} — **"these are the four spirits of the heavens"** (angelic decode)
- {{ref:Zec.6.6-7}} — dispatched north, south, to and fro
- {{ref:Zec.6.8}} — "have quieted my spirit in the north country"

### Four seals — sequential judgment release (Revelation)
- {{ref:Rev.6.1-2}} — white horse: bow, crown, conquering
- {{ref:Rev.6.3-4}} — red horse: great sword, takes peace from earth
- {{ref:Rev.6.5-6}} — black horse: balances, famine pricing
- {{ref:Rev.6.7-8}} — pale horse: Death rides, Hades follows; sword + hunger + death + beasts

### Four winds restrained then released
- {{ref:Rev.7.1-3}} — four angels hold four winds until servants sealed
- {{ref:Dan.7.2-3}} — four winds strive upon the sea → four beast-kingdoms rise
- {{ref:Jer.49.36}} — "four winds from the four quarters of heaven" scattered upon Elam

### The four covenant judgments (Ezekiel source)
- {{ref:Eze.14.21}} — sword, famine, noisome beast, pestilence

### Olivet Discourse parallel
- {{ref:Mat.24.4-5}} — deception / false Christs (→ seal 1)
- {{ref:Mat.24.6}} — wars and rumors of wars (→ seal 2)
- {{ref:Mat.24.7}} — famines, pestilences, earthquakes (→ seals 3-4)
- {{ref:Mat.24.8}} — "the beginning of birth pains"

### Spirits = angels = winds
- {{ref:Ps.104.4}} — "who maketh his angels spirits, his ministers a flaming fire"

### Christ on white horse (distinct from seal 1)
- {{ref:Rev.19.11}} — rider called "Faithful and True," sword from mouth, judges in righteousness

